# Operator instructions and delegation

## Prefer execution in this workspace

When the task can be completed **in this repo environment** (read/write files, run terminal commands, tests, builds, greps), **do it** instead of only listing steps for the user.

## Copy-paste blocks for anything they must run elsewhere

When steps **cannot** be done here (SSH to Droplet, DigitalOcean/Slack/browser UIs, typing secrets):

1. Use **numbered steps** and **full, runnable commands** — complete paths, no `...` omissions in commands meant for paste.
2. One **fenced code block** per paste (or clearly separated blocks) so the user can copy in order.
3. State **where** to run each block (e.g. “on the Droplet, repo root: `/opt/parking-acquisition-agents`”).

## Do not

- Rely on “run the usual command” or partial commands when a full command is what they need to paste.
- Dump long prose checklists without equivalent copy-paste commands when commands exist.

The user is not technical; minimize manual interpretation.
